  "decision": "keep",
  "effect": "blocked_target_coverage",
  "reason": "The after source supports preserving CHARBOUND markers for graphemes retained by STRIPCC. Mapping is a primary target operation, but the fixed harness has no map call combining those options. The same preservation behavior was unavailable before the change, so this coverage gap is introduced. Evidence: u-c2ddb5ea0940cb0a5374:641-650, u-82fb367dcb7283a12bb8:641-646, u-1f26bb9c4ca01b89207f:78-97.",
  "finite_witness": "Valid input bytes {0x61, 0x01, 0x62, 0x00} pass the entry's size and terminator gates. With the supported setup CHARBOUND|STRIPCC, mapping strips U+0001 and preserves a boundary marker before each retained letter, yielding {0xff, 0x61, 0xff, 0x62, 0x00}. The fixed harness supplies that input to map calls, but none uses both options.",
  "scope_contract": {
    "status": "established",
    "reason": "The entry primarily maps text, including CHARBOUND mappings. The source defines CHARBOUND markers and STRIPCC control stripping as options on that mapping surface.",
